From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 07:30:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH qemu-server] vmstatus: flag host-side memory fallback for
 guests without balloon stats

vmstatus() seeds $d->{mem} from the cgroup and lets the balloon callback
override it, but the override only happens when query-balloon carries
total_mem and free_mem:

    $d->{mem} = $d->{memhost};   # default to cgroup, balloon info can override this below
    ...
    if (defined($info->{total_mem}) && defined($info->{free_mem})) {
        $d->{mem} = $info->{total_mem} - $info->{free_mem};
        $d->{freemem} = $info->{free_mem};
    }

A guest whose balloon driver does not implement the statistics virtqueue
never supplies those. FreeBSD's vtballoon(4) is the common case - it
attaches, but never negotiates VIRTIO_BALLOON_F_STATS_VQ - which covers
every FreeBSD-based guest, OPNsense and pfSense included.

Two guests on one host, via query-balloon:

  # Ubuntu 26.04, 5 GB assigned
  balloon: actual=5056 max_mem=5056 total_mem=4335 free_mem=3342 \
           ... last_update=1795323645

  # OPNsense 26.7 (FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE-p1), 20 GB assigned
  balloon: actual=20480 max_mem=20480

For the second, 'mem' silently stays at the cgroup figure, so the guest is
reported as using its full allocation forever. Because that figure includes
QEMU's own overhead it can exceed maxmem - observed 100.23% of a 4 GiB VM -
while the guest itself reported under 1 GB in use. The UI has no way to tell
this apart from a genuine out-of-memory situation and renders it critical.

Nothing can be done about the missing data here; the fix belongs in the guest
driver, and one is pending upstream [1]. But 'mem' being a host-side estimate
rather than a guest measurement is knowable, so record it instead of letting
consumers guess. No existing behaviour changes: the new field is only set on
the path that was already falling back.

A follow-up in pve-manager can then label the value and skip the critical
threshold for it.

[1] https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-src/pull/2509
    "virtio_balloon: Add memory statistics queue support"

Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@example.com>
---
 PVE/QemuServer.pm | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/PVE/QemuServer.pm
+++ b/PVE/QemuServer.pm
@@ -2355,6 +2355,15 @@
         optional => 1,
         renderer => 'bytes',
     },
+    memfallback => {
+        description => "Set when 'mem' could not be obtained from the guest and falls back"
+            . " to the host-side figure, because the guest's balloon driver does not"
+            . " implement the statistics virtqueue. Such a value includes QEMU's own"
+            . " overhead and may exceed 'maxmem'; it should not be presented as guest"
+            . " memory usage.",
+        type => 'boolean',
+        optional => 1,
+    },
     maxdisk => {
         description => "Root disk size in bytes.",
         type => 'integer',
@@ -2651,6 +2660,14 @@
         if (defined($info->{total_mem}) && defined($info->{free_mem})) {
             $d->{mem} = $info->{total_mem} - $info->{free_mem};
             $d->{freemem} = $info->{free_mem};
+        } else {
+            # The guest's balloon driver does not implement the statistics
+            # virtqueue - FreeBSD's vtballoon(4) attaches but never negotiates
+            # VIRTIO_BALLOON_F_STATS_VQ - so query-balloon carries only actual
+            # and max_mem, and $d->{mem} keeps the cgroup value set above.
+            # That is a host-side figure including QEMU's own overhead, which
+            # can push it past maxmem; let consumers tell the two apart.
+            $d->{memfallback} = 1;
         }

         $d->{ballooninfo} = $info;
